    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q1-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Bag A contains 3 red balls and 4 green balls and bag B contains 2 red balls and 3 green balls. A fair dice numbered 1 to 6 is rolled. • If the dice shows 6 , a ball is drawn at random from bag A . • If the dice does not show 6 , a ball is drawn at random from bag B . a) Find the probability that a red ball will be drawn. ( ) 3 b) Given that a red ball was drawn, determine the probability that the dice had previously shown a six. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:606.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
