    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-n/q2",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q2-question-1.svg\" alt=\"An airline operates between Manchester and Madrid. The flight time may be modelled by a Normal distribution with mean of 85 minutes and standard deviation 8 . In order to boost sales for the service, the airline decides to refund the fares if a flight time exceeds the mean flight time by t minutes. The airline does not want to refund more than 0.005 of the fares. Find the value of t , correct to the nearest minute. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:601.5px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q2-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"For X ∼N(85, 82), the limiting threshold satisfies P(X ≤85 + t) = 0.995. [M1] The upper-tail limit is 0.005, leaving 1 −0.005 = 0.995 below the cutoff: Standardising gives (85 + t −85)/8 = t/8, whose inverse-normal value is 2.5758 . . .. Thus t = 8Φ−1(0.995) ≈20.6066 min. [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"To the nearest minute the threshold is 21 min . [M1] [A1] It also meets the limit if the threshold must be a whole number of minutes: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 2 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "An airline operates between Manchester and Madrid. The flight time may be modelled by a Normal distribution with mean of 85 minutes and standard deviation 8 . In order to boost sales for the service, the airline decides to refund the fares if a flight time exceeds the mean flight time by t minutes. The airline does not want to refund more than 0.005 of the fares. Find the value of t , correct to the nearest minute. ( ) 6"
