    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A farmer keeps chicken and sells most of the eggs they lay. The table below summarizes information about the number of eggs laid by his chickens every week, for a period of 47 weeks. Total number of eggs laid in a week Number of weeks 52 1 53 4 54 7 55 10 56 11 57 8 58 5 59 1\" style=\"--madas-width:565.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q3-question-2.svg\" alt=\"a) Calculate the mean and the standard deviation of the eggs laid per week. ( ) 5 b) Determine the median and the quartiles for these data. ( ) 3 c) If the farmer only sells 45 eggs per week and keeps the rest for his family, find the mean and the standard deviation of the eggs he keeps for his family. ( ) 3 d) Use the median and mean to determine the skew of the above data, and hence determine whether this data can be modelled by a Normal distribution. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:589.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The weighted totals are fx2 = 145391. X X X f = 47, fx = 2613, [B1] The mean is 55.596 [M1] [A1] and the standard deviation is q 145391/47 −(2613/47)2 ≈1.593 . [M1] [A1] (b) With 47 observations the three positions are (47 + 1)/4 = 12, (47 + 1)/2 = 24, 3(47 + 1)/4 = 36. The 12th, 24th and 36th ordered values are 54, 56, 57 , [M1] [A1] respectively: [A1] (c) Subtracting 45 from every observation lowers the mean by 45 and keeps the spread fixed: [M1] The mean and standard deviation are 10.596, 1.593 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(d) The mean is below the median, suggesting negative skew: [B1] [A1] A symmetric normal distribution would only be an approximation, and the mean and median alone cannot determine how good that approximation is: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 14 marks.</p>"
