    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-n/q6",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q6-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The records in a doctor’s surgery show that 20% of the patients that make an appointment fail to turn up. During a given weekday there are 20 appointments to see the doctor and the doctor has enough time to see all 20 patients. a) Find the probability that all the patients will turn up. ( ) 2 b) Find the probability that more than three patients will not turn up. ( ) 2 In order to improve efficiency in the surgery, the doctor decides to make more than 20 appointments although he still has enough time to see only 20 patients. One day the doctor has booked 21 appointments.\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q6-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) Find the probability he will be able to see all the patients that will turn up. ( ) 3 Another day the doctor has booked 25 appointments. d) Find the probability that the doctor will not be able to see one of the patients that will turn up. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:581.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q6-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Assuming independent attendance decisions, the number of missed appointments among n bookings follows B(n, 0.2). (a) With 20 bookings, P(X = 0) = 0.820 ≈0.0115 . [M1] [A1] (b) P(X &gt; 3) = 1 −P(X ≤3) ≈0.5886 . [M1] [A1] (c) With 21 bookings he requires at least one absence: [M1] The probability is 1 −0.821 ≈0.9908 . [M1] [A1] (d) Having more than 20 arrivals means 25 −X &gt; 20, giving X &lt; 5. Exactly five absences would leave just enough capacity: With 25 bookings demand exceeds capacity if there are at most four absences: [M1] The probability is\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"P(X ≤4) ≈0.4207 [A1] for X ∼B(25, 0.2). [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
