    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-n/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"B C 60° A\" style=\"--madas-width:405.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q9-question-2.svg\" alt=\"A uniform ladder AB , of length 6 m  and mass 20 kg , is placed with its end A on rough horizontal ground and B over a smooth vertical wall. The ladder rests on the wall at the point C , so that BC = 1 m . The ladder is inclined at an angle of  60° to the horizontal and the coefficient of friction between the ladder and the ground is µ . When a man, of mass 80 kg , is standing at the point P on the ladder, so that AP = 4 m , the ladder is in limiting equilibrium. Determine the exact value of µ . ( ) 9\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a good diagram in order to form some equations:\" style=\"--madas-width:486.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The smooth upper edge exerts a reaction N perpendicular to the ladder: [B1] [A1] Taking moments about A gives 5N = (20g · 3 + 80g · 4) cos 60◦, [M1] [A1] hence N = 38g. [A1] Evaluate the clockwise moment as (60g + 320g)/2 = 190g; hence N = 190g/5 . = 38g Horizontally the limiting friction balances √ N sin 60◦= 19 3 g. [A1] The ground’s normal reaction is R = 100g −N cos 60◦ . [A1] = 81g Therefore √ µ = 19 3/81 . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 9 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "B C 60° A A uniform ladder AB , of length 6 m  and mass 20 kg , is placed with its end A on rough horizontal ground and B over a smooth vertical wall. The ladder rests on the wall at the point C , so that BC = 1 m . The ladder is inclined at an angle of  60° to the horizontal and the coefficient of friction between the ladder and the ground is µ . When a man, of mass 80 kg , is standing at the point P on the ladder, so that AP = 4 m , the ladder is in limiting equilibrium. Determine the exact value of µ . ( ) 9"
