    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle is moving in a straight line in an electromagnetic field. ms−, at time t s , 1 Its velocity, v t ≥ 0 , is given by 2 v = t + kt + 3.2 , where k is a non zero constant. a) Given that the particle achieves its minimum velocity when t = 2.4 s , show that k = − 4.8 . ( ) 2 b) Determine the values of t when the particle is instantaneously at rest. ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q10-question-2.svg\" alt=\"c) Calculate the total distance covered by the particle for 0 ( ) ≤≤ t 6 . 8\" style=\"--madas-width:578.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) At the minimum, v′(2.4) = 2(2.4) + k , [M1] = 0 so k = −4.8 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) Now v = (t −0.8)(t −4). [B1] Rest occurs at 0.8 s [M1] [A1] and 4 s . [A1] (c) Velocity is positive before 0.8, negative between 0.8 and 4, and positive after 4. [B1] [M1] [A1] An antiderivative is F(t) = t3/3 −2.4t2 + 3.2t. [M1] [A1] Evaluate the primitive at the turning points: F(0) = 0, F(0.8) = 448/375, F(4) = −64/15, F(6) = 24/5. Reverse the sign of the middle signed area where the motion is backwards: The total distance is [F(0.8) −F(0)] + [F(0.8) −F(4)] + [F(6) −F(4)] ≈15.723 m . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 14 marks.</p>"
    ],
