    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at the diagram below: (a) The speed of A is √ q 65 km h−1 . 42 + (−7)2 = [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) Ship B moves west of north at arctan(2/5) ≈21.8◦. [M1] Its bearing is 338.2◦. [A1] (c) The initial relative position is −12i + 4j and relative velocity is 6i −12j. Thus the position of A relative to B is (6t −12)i + (4 −12t)j [A1] in kilometres: [A1] (d) The squared magnitude is (6t −12)2 + (4 −12t)2 = 180t2 −240t + 160 . [M1] [M1] [A1] (e) Set d2 = 100, [M1] which gives 3t2 −4t + 1 = (3t −1)(t −1) . [A1] = 0\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q14-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Thus the times are 12:20 p.m. [A1] and 1:00 p.m. . [A1] (f) Completing the square gives d2 = 180(t −2 3)2 + 80. [B1] Alternatively minimise d2 by differentiating: The derivative 360t −240 vanishes at t = 2/3 hours, and the positive second derivative 360 confirms the minimum. Substitution gives d2 = 80. The shortest distance is √ 4 5 km ≈8.94 km . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 14 is 16 marks.</p>"
