      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-n/q15-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Their trapezium areas are 1 2(4 + 4 + 0.8t)t and 1 2(10 + 10 + 0.2t)t. Subtract the second area from the first and set it equal to 240. Hence 0.3t2 −6t = 240, (t −40)(t + 20) = 0. [M1] [A1] Only the nonnegative root is relevant, so t = 40 s . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
